Z||000000||Jeff's '86 1/2 GT||10-13-2000||02:42 PM||||<BR>Well the 86 GT has been in the family since brade new.  We love her, but might need to get rid of her and walk away for Fiero's if no one is able to help us.  Problem, is there was a small fire under the hood, a couple of weeks ago.   Well, It needed Throttle Cable, Return Spring, Cruise Control Cable,  rubber garments and wires.   Well it goes down to the Dealership  to be worked on, and I am told that Return Spring in Discontinued, as is the Cruise Control Cable, and rubber garments.  They also tell me that my E Brake is lose, and that is discontinued also.  They never found what started the fire, so I don't know if that will happen again or not.   Does anyone have these parts??  What is with everything being discontinued??  This was a very nice car, and now is a piece of junk.  It is barely drivable now, and I am out $491.  So plaese help me find these parts, and  how to fix it myself.   Thank you for all help.   I did LOVE this car, but now I just want to sell it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Patrick||10-13-2000||02:59 PM||||<BR>Sounds to me like the biggest problem you encountered is having taken the Fiero into a <I>dealership</I> to be worked on. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>There's several people at this forum who deal in used parts for Fieros. I'm sure that one or two of them will be able to set you straight for a fraction of the price that a dealership would want to charge.<P>It might be a good idea to determine why that fire started before any repairs are made though!||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||10-13-2000||03:36 PM||||Jeff,  If you a close to Sacramento, there are three pick-n-pull yards (Rocklin, Rancho Cordova, South Sac)  that all have V6 Fieros in them right now.  I know the one in Rocklin/Roseville has two cars with a large part if the engine bay still intact (one was hit from behind so it may not have all you need).  You should be able to get everything you need from these three yards.  If not there is always Kick Hill farms, FieroShop (Richmond), and I have a couple of other contacts in the area that may have additional parts.||||reg||1
